IMPORT prelude
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §11.0.1, "Stacking B on C (2026-09-16)": the
-- anchored WITHIN (R-Q7B, §5.1.1.1) on top of the blame set (R-T3, §6.1.1).
--
-- C: a barrier's LEST fires ONCE for the group, anchored at the EARLIEST
-- failure by R-Q5 — the member's act deadline for MUST/DO/MAY, the violating
-- stamp for SHANT — with that member's residual stream. B: a continuation
-- reads THE DEADLINE from the obligation it is attached to; under a
-- barrier's LEST that is the deadline a member missed.
--
-- Stacked, these must name the SAME member: THE DEADLINE under a barrier's
-- LEST is the deadline of the member whose failure the LEST is anchored at
-- — the earliest failure — wherever that member stands on the roll, and
-- also when two misses come to light at the same event (then the earlier
-- deadline wins the tie, not the earlier roll position). Every trace below
-- pins the number that rule produces; the comment says what a different
-- rule would have produced instead.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Refund  HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Smoke   HAS who    IS AN Actor

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
carol       MEANS Tenant OF "Carol"
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob, carol
`tenants, reversed` MEANS LIST carol, bob, alice

-- Carol, LAST on the roll, has the EARLIEST deadline (5); Bob, before her,
-- has 14; Alice too.
GIVEN t IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days allowed to` t MEANS IF t EQUALS carol THEN 5 ELSE 14


§ `1. the last member on the roll fails first: THE DEADLINE is hers`

-- Alice signs at 1. Carol misses 5 (revealed by WAIT UNTIL 8); Bob misses
-- 14 (revealed by WAIT UNTIL 20). The LEST is anchored at Carol's failure
-- (revealed at 8, before Bob's at 20), and THE DEADLINE under it is CAROL's,
-- 5: the refund is due 5 + 5 = 10. A refund at 10 is timely; at 11 the
-- breach reports 10. Were THE DEADLINE Bob's — first on the roll to fail,
-- 14 — the refund would be due 19 and both refunds would be timely.
GIVEN roll IS A LIST OF Actor
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`staggered` roll MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN roll
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN `days allowed to` t
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `staggered` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 10
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `staggered` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)


§ `2. the roll reversed: the same member, the same deadline`

-- Carol is now FIRST on the roll. Same events, same answer: due 10.
#TRACE `staggered` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 10
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `staggered` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)


§ `3. a tie: both misses revealed by the SAME event`

-- Nothing happens between Carol's deadline (5) and Bob's (14): WAIT UNTIL 20
-- reveals both at once. The LEST's anchor (the revealing stamp, 20) and its
-- residual stream are the same whichever member is chosen, so for the blame
-- set alone the tie did not matter; THE DEADLINE is 5 or 14 depending on
-- it. The earliest failure by R-Q5 is Carol's (5 < 14) from either roll, so
-- the tie is broken by the deadline missed and the refund at 21 reports
-- 5 + 5 = 10 on BOTH rolls. (Broken by roll order it reported 19 on
-- `tenants` and 10 on `tenants, reversed` — measured 2026-09-16 before the
-- tie-break was added.)
#TRACE `staggered` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 21

#TRACE `staggered` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 21


§ `4. SHANT: the violating stamp orders, the window's end is THE DEADLINE`

-- A prohibition barrier. Carol's window ends at 5, Bob's at 14. Carol smokes
-- at 3 (failure time 3 by R-Q5), Bob at 10 (failure time 10); Alice keeps
-- hers. The LEST is anchored at Carol's violation (3 < 10) and THE DEADLINE
-- under it is Carol's window end, 5 — what a single SHANT's LEST is handed
-- — so the refund is due 5 + 5 = 10: at 10 FULFILLED, at 11 BREACHED
-- reporting 10. The same on the reversed roll.
GIVEN roll IS A LIST OF Actor
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`no smoking` roll MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN roll
        SHANT  Smoke (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN `days allowed to` t
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `no smoking` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY carol DOES Smoke carol AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 10
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 10
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `no smoking` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY carol DOES Smoke carol AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 10
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `no smoking` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY carol DOES Smoke carol AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 10
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)


§ `5. RAND of two anchored continuations, both breached`

-- Alice signs at 4: the join is 4, THE DEADLINE 10. The landlord's delivery
-- is due 10 + 5 = 15 (OF THE DEADLINE); Bob's signature 4 + 3 = 7 (OF THE
-- JOIN). Neither happens; WAIT UNTIL 20 reveals both at once. The RAND is
-- anchored at the first breach — a tie at 20, so the LEFT operand — and it
-- names BOTH failures, left first, each with the deadline its anchor
-- produced: the landlord's 15, then Bob's 7.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`both anchored` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 10
    HENCE ((PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)
           RAND (PARTY bob MUST Sign (EXACTLY bob) WITHIN 3 OF THE JOIN))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `both anchored` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
